Roger stone is flamboyant a provocateur  and the man who shaped Donald Trump's  political image and encouraged him to  run for president  he's also been a close personal friend  of the president for decades so when  federal prosecutors from the Justice  Department recommended stone served  seven to nine years in prison Trump took  the unusual step of intervening in the  case I think it's a disgrace stone was  caught up in Special Counsel Robert  Muller's investigation into Russian  interference in the 2016 election a  grand jury indicted stone on seven  counts including witness tampering and  lying to investigators prosecutors also  accused him of threatening witnesses  stone was found guilty last year and is  awaiting sentencing on Tuesday Trump  tweeted the sentencing recommendation of  seven to nine years was a miscarriage of  justice later in the day the Justice  Department revised its recommendation  for sentencing prompting criticism that  the president was abusing his powers no  I have not been involved with it at all  by Tuesday evening all four federal  prosecutors here at the Justice  Department that were working the case  have reportedly stepped down in protest  and the top Democrat in the Senate is  accusing the president of acting  inappropriately Roger stone should get  the full amount of time the prosecutors  recommended it all comes less than a  week after the president was acquitted  by the Senate on charges of obstruction  of Congress and abuse of power  some critics now feel the president  feels emboldened by the acquittal so  he's basically saying he will wield the  instruments of power to favor his  political friends and punish his  political enemies Trump voters likely  won't see this as the president doing  anything wrong  however Democrats in Congress might see  otherwise and argue it's another example  of the president getting involved in  something he shouldn't Gabriel as andö  al Jazeera Washington
 

